        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-04T23:54:40.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Pydro\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/48/1844_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Pydro:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Who's Your Con is also going to have one.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes, Who's Yer Con (Indianapolis, Apr 17-18,&nbsp;<a href=\"http://whosyergamers.org/wyc.php\">http://whosyergamers.org/wyc.php</a>) is having an UNOFFICIAL tournament. GtG has provided a prize for the champion (painted minis), but winners will not be eligible for the championship tournament at GenCon 2015.</p>",
